'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... test_bench_char.spin2
''   Purpose.... Unattended, meter-free motor characterisation -- quarter/half speed, both motors,
''               both increment signs, every reading taken from the driver's own telemetry
''   Authors.... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- Copyright (c) 2026 Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... 11 Sep 2026
''   Updated.... 13 Sep 2026 -- task 3521 phase A: unattended automatic holds (no PLOT panel, no
''               operator advance, no dwell floor), same-lifetime zero per hold (PL-32), overflow-
''               proof accumulators (PL-20), quiescent hold from a started driver (PL-21), booleans
''               as TRUE/FALSE (PL-23), motor frame named on every hold (PL-19), no method-calling
''               ternaries (PL-29)
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ WHY THIS RUN

  Bench Pass 1 (DOCs/analyses/bench/2026-09-12/CHAR-RUN-EVALUATION.md) ran this binary as an
  operator-held, meter-read session. The current channel is now confirmed (sense_i_mV is true
  millivolts, about 150 mV/A on Rev B), so every hold is now measured from the driver's own
  telemetry, unattended, with no meter and no keypress.

  FRAME. Every hold is in MOTOR frame: the signed motor increment is what is commanded, and
  forwardIsReverse() is never called on either wheel. Every BC-HOLD record carries the signed
  increment, a robot_dir field (LEFT + = robot forward, RIGHT + = robot reverse, because the two
  motors are mounted mirror-image), and frame,MOTOR. Every caption names its frame (PL-19).

  THE IDLE WHEEL IS NEVER RUNNING. Each hold stop()s both wheels and then start()s only the wheel
  under test, so the other wheel has no driver cog, its pins are released and its bridges float.
  holdAtStop() appears nowhere; init()'s default SM_FLOAT gives a floating stop.

  EACH HOLD IS ITS OWN DRIVER LIFETIME. The driver calibrates its ADCs at start (PL-32), so a sense
  zero is valid only within the lifetime it was read in. Every hold, including the quiescent hold
  0, starts its wheel, then reads its own zero at zero command, then measures -- never a zero from
  before a restart.

  HOLD SEQUENCE (per motion hold):
   (1) stop both wheels, start the hold's wheel, wait ready (READY_TIMEOUT_MS), startSenseCog()
   (2) zero: ZERO_SAMPLES x SAMPLE_MS at zero command, same lifetime
   (3) command the signed increment, wait DCS_AT_SPEED (ATSPEED_TIMEOUT_MS), waitForSteady()
       (hall-rate confirmation, STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS), settle SETTLE_MS
   (4) sample every SAMPLE_MS for WINDOW_MS; testGetRpm() read at the window's end, which is at
       least SETTLE_MS + WINDOW_MS = 4 s after AT_SPEED (rpm needs ~1 s of motion to fill)
   (5) command zero, wait STOPPED (STOP_TIMEOUT_MS), stop the wheel, and ONLY THEN print
  Hold 0 is steps (1), (2), (4) and (5) on HOLD_ZERO_SIDE, started and held at zero command.
  A bounded wait that times out becomes that hold's result token; it never aborts the run.

  NO timed window (zero, AT_SPEED wait, steady wait, settle, sample window, stop wait) contains a
  debug() statement or a call to a library method that emits one. Every record is emitted after
  the wheel has stopped.

  NO STOP TIMER. Motion is commanded with testDriveAtMotorIncrement() alone; stopAfterTime() is
  never called, so the sense task never zeroes a command behind this file's back.

  PANIC PROCEDURE IS PHYSICAL BATTERY DISCONNECT ONLY. emergencyCutoff() self-cancels in about
  250 ms (finding S-4) and is NOT a panic button; this file does not call it.

  HOW IT IS RUN

      tools/bench-run.sh char

  -D BENCH_CFG selects isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench.spin2 for the banner's cfg_id only -- the
  pin bases, voltage and detection mode this file drives are compile-time constants (CON
  { bench target }) so it compiles under every block of isp_bldc_motor_userconfig.spin2.

  RECORD DISCIPLINE

  Tag-first, comma-separated name,value pairs, all tags prefixed BC-. Every record type always
  emits every field in the same order; absence is the token NA, never a missing field and never
  a 0. Booleans are the tokens TRUE/FALSE (PL-23). Every numeric field is clamped to a stated
  width and every token to a stated length, so each record's worst case is a stated number of
  bytes under 280 (the longest record measured intact through one debug(zstr_())). The worst
  case of each record is stated at its emitter.
}

CON { build identity }

    SRC_REV     = 2                                         ' hand-bumped whenever this file changes
    FMT_VERSION = 2                                         ' BC- record-format version (2: task 3521 phase A)

CON { timing }

    CLK_FREQ = 270_000_000                                  ' every top in this tree runs at 270 MHz
    _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ
    MS_PER_SEC = 1000

CON { bench target -- the fixed dual 6.5in Rev B 18.5V rig }

' Hardcoded rather than read from `user`: a dual-motor config block defines LEFT_MOTOR_BASE /
' RIGHT_MOTOR_BASE and no ONLY_MOTOR_BASE, and vice versa, so reading either through `user`
' would fail to compile under whichever block is active. The library's own PINS_*/PWR_*/BRD_*
' constants are legal under every config block.
    LEFT_TEST_BASE  = wheelL.PINS_P32_P47                    ' the LEFT board is at P32, measured 2026-09-11
    RIGHT_TEST_BASE = wheelL.PINS_P16_P31
    TEST_VOLTAGE    = wheelL.PWR_18p5V
    TEST_DET_MODE   = wheelL.BRD_AUTO_DET
    MAX_COG_ID      = 7                                      ' start() returns a cog id 0..7, or -1

CON { drive speed -- NO increment may exceed DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE }

' isp_bldc_motor.spin2 confgurePowerLimits(): 147_000_000 is the 18.5V motor-increment ceiling.
    DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE = 147_000_000
    QTR_SPEED_INCRE     = DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE / 4           ' 36_750_000, quarter speed
    HALF_SPEED_INCRE    = DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE / 2           ' 73_500_000, half speed
    PREFLIGHT_INCRE     = DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE / 8           ' 18_375_000, gentle nudge

CON { sampling, windows and wait bounds }

    SAMPLE_MS          = 5                                  ' telemetry poll cadence in every timed loop
    ZERO_SAMPLES       = 200                                ' same-lifetime zero: 200 x 5 ms, ~1 s
    SETTLE_MS          = 1_000                              ' after AT_SPEED (and the rate check), before the window
    ' WINDOW_MS: 3 s at ~99 ticks/s (quarter speed) is ~297 hall ticks, just over 3 wheel
    ' revolutions (90 ticks/rev) -- the same span the offset scan uses for a fine point
    ' (WIN_TICKS_FINE = 270) -- so the mean averages whole revolutions of hall/cogging ripple
    ' rather than a fraction of one; ~600 samples at SAMPLE_MS. It also exceeds the ~1 s rpm
    ' averaging window, so testGetRpm() at its end reads a full window of steady motion.
    WINDOW_MS          = 3_000
    READY_TIMEOUT_MS   = 2_000                              ' driver cog reports ready after start()
    ATSPEED_TIMEOUT_MS = 4_000                              ' AT_SPEED observed ~0.9 s (1/4) / ~1.3 s (1/2) in the scan
    STOP_TIMEOUT_MS    = 3_000                              ' ramp-down ~0.37 s (1/4) / ~0.75 s (1/2)
    STEADY_SAMPLE_MS   = 250                                ' waitForSteady() hall-rate sample period
    STEADY_CONFIRM_SAMPLES = 4
    STEADY_TOL_PCT     = 5
    STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS  = 6_000                              ' waitForSteady() bound
    PREFLIGHT_MS       = 700                                ' preflight nudge duration per wheel
    RATE_X10_SCALE     = 10_000                             ' ticks * this / ms = ticks per second x10
    RATE_TICKS_CAP     = 99_999                             ' ticks clamp before * RATE_X10_SCALE: 999_990_000 < 2^31
    X10                = 10

CON { overflow-proof running mean (PL-20) }

' Every accumulator is an EXACT incremental mean held as (mean, remainder, count), with the
' invariant  sum == mean * count + remainder,  0 <= remainder < count  -- the true sum is never
' stored, so it cannot overflow however long the window runs or however large the scale.
' Adding sample x (clamped to +/-ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT) at new count n computes
'     delta = remainder + x - mean
' and then mean += floor(delta / n), remainder = delta - floor(delta / n) * n.
' Bound: remainder < n <= ACC_COUNT_CAP, |x| <= ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT, and |mean| <= ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT
' (a floor mean of clamped samples), so
'     |delta| < ACC_COUNT_CAP + 2 * ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT = 100_000_000 + 1_000_000_000
'             = 1_100_000_000  <  2_147_483_647 (POSX).
' ACC_COUNT_CAP at SAMPLE_MS = 5 ms is 500_000 s (~5.8 days) of samples; past it further samples
' are not added (the count stops, so the record still states how many samples the mean holds).
' ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT is ~100x the pre-S-3 scale's largest reading (~5.2e6 mV), so no real sample
' is ever clamped. The x10 mean is (mean clamped to +/-ACC_MEAN_X10_LIMIT) * 10 + remainder * 10
' / count, where remainder * 10 < ACC_COUNT_CAP * 10 = 1e9 < POSX.
    ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT   = 500_000_000
    ACC_COUNT_CAP      = 100_000_000
    ACC_MEAN_X10_LIMIT = 99_999_999

  ' Accumulator slots:
  '  ACC_ZERO  - sense_i_mV at zero command, same driver lifetime
  '  ACC_SENSE - sense_i_mV over the sample window
  '  ACC_AMPS  - getCurrent() amps x 10_000 over the window
  '  ACC_WATTS - getCurrent() mW over the window
  '  ACC_DUTY  - duty over the window
  '  ACC_ERR   - position error over the window
    #0, ACC_ZERO, ACC_SENSE, ACC_AMPS, ACC_WATTS, ACC_DUTY, ACC_ERR
    ACC_SLOTS = ACC_ERR + 1

CON ' ---- Hold Sequence ----
  ' The nine-hold run: quiescent zero, then left/right x +/- increment at quarter speed, then
  ' left/right x +/- again at half speed. HOLD_LAST selects how far the run goes.
    #0, HOLD_ZERO, HOLD_L_FWD_QTR, HOLD_L_REV_QTR, HOLD_R_FWD_QTR, HOLD_R_REV_QTR, ...
        HOLD_L_FWD_HALF, HOLD_L_REV_HALF, HOLD_R_FWD_HALF, HOLD_R_REV_HALF
    HOLD_COUNT = HOLD_R_REV_HALF + 1
    HOLD_LAST  = HOLD_R_REV_HALF                            ' edit to stop the run earlier
    HOLD_ZERO_SIDE = SIDE_LEFT                              ' hold 0's driver: LEFT, started at zero command (PL-21)

CON ' ---- Motor-Side / Result Enums ----
  ' Which wheel a hold drives:
  '  SIDE_NONE  - no wheel
  '  SIDE_LEFT  - wheelL started, wheelR not running
  '  SIDE_RIGHT - wheelR started, wheelL not running
    #0, SIDE_NONE, SIDE_LEFT, SIDE_RIGHT

  ' Hold result (the first cause is kept, except that a fault or a lost cog always overwrites):
  '  RES_OK             - every step completed
  '  RES_NOT_RUN        - the hold was never reached
  '  RES_NO_COG         - start() failed, or the driver cog was not running when read
  '  RES_READY_TIMEOUT  - the driver did not report ready within READY_TIMEOUT_MS
  '  RES_STEADY_TIMEOUT - DCS_AT_SPEED not reached within ATSPEED_TIMEOUT_MS
  '  RES_FAULT          - the driver faulted
  '  RES_STOP_TIMEOUT   - STOPPED not reached within STOP_TIMEOUT_MS after the zero command
    #0, RES_OK, RES_NOT_RUN, RES_NO_COG, RES_READY_TIMEOUT, RES_STEADY_TIMEOUT, ...
        RES_FAULT, RES_STOP_TIMEOUT

CON { record widths -- every numeric field is clamped to one of these }

    LIM_TINY  = 999                                         ' prints at most 4 bytes: -999
    LIM_SMALL = 99_999                                      ' prints at most 7 bytes: -99_999
    LIM_MID   = 9_999_999                                   ' prints at most 10 bytes: -9_999_999
    LIM_BIG   = 999_999_999                                 ' prints at most 12 bytes: -999_999_999

    ' token field length limits (a longer token prints as "?")
    TOKMAX_MOTOR   = 5
    TOKMAX_ROBOT   = 4
    TOKMAX_FRAME   = 5
    TOKMAX_RUNG    = 4
    TOKMAX_RESULT  = 14
    TOKMAX_STEADY  = 7
    TOKMAX_CFG     = 5
    TOKMAX_BOARD   = 7
    TOKMAX_EXIT    = 8
    TOKMAX_CAPTION = 96

CON { record assembly buffer }

    LINE_BUF_SIZE    = 640
    MAX_DEC_DIGITS   = 11
    DEC_RADIX        = 10
    DIGITS_PER_GROUP = 3

OBJ { objects under test }

#ifdef BENCH_CFG
    user   : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig_bench"              ' banner cfg_id only -- see CON { bench target }
#else
    user   : "isp_bldc_motor_userconfig"
#endif
    wheelL : "isp_bldc_motor"                                ' left wheel instance
    wheelR : "isp_bldc_motor"                                ' right wheel instance

DAT { record assembly state }

lineBuf         BYTE    0[LINE_BUF_SIZE]
lineLen         LONG    0

DAT { token strings }

sNa             BYTE    "NA", 0
sTrue           BYTE    "TRUE", 0
sFalse          BYTE    "FALSE", 0
sBadTok         BYTE    "?", 0

sMotNone        BYTE    "NONE", 0
sMotLeft        BYTE    "LEFT", 0
sMotRight       BYTE    "RIGHT", 0

sRobotNone      BYTE    "NONE", 0
sRobotFwd       BYTE    "FWD", 0
sRobotRev       BYTE    "REV", 0

sRungZero       BYTE    "ZERO", 0
sRungQtr        BYTE    "QTR", 0
sRungHalf       BYTE    "HALF", 0

sSteadyRamped   BYTE    "RAMPED", 0
sSteadyTimeout  BYTE    "TIMEOUT", 0
sSteadyZerocmd  BYTE    "ZEROCMD", 0

sResOk          BYTE    "OK", 0
sResNotRun      BYTE    "NOT_RUN", 0
sResNoCog       BYTE    "NO_COG", 0
sResReadyTo     BYTE    "READY_TIMEOUT", 0
sResSteadyTo    BYTE    "STEADY_TIMEOUT", 0
sResFault       BYTE    "FAULT", 0
sResStopTo      BYTE    "STOP_TIMEOUT", 0

sCfgBench       BYTE    "BENCH", 0
sCfgUser        BYTE    "USER", 0
sFrameMotor     BYTE    "MOTOR", 0

sBoardRevA      BYTE    "REV_A", 0
sBoardRevB      BYTE    "REV_B", 0
sBoardUnknown   BYTE    "UNKNOWN", 0

sExitComplete   BYTE    "COMPLETE", 0
sExitAborted    BYTE    "ABORTED", 0

DAT { hold caption strings -- every caption names its frame (PL-19) }

sHold0Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 1 of 9 - QUIESCENT ZERO - LEFT MOTOR STARTED AT ZERO COMMAND (motor frame)", 0
sHold1Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 2 of 9 - LEFT MOTOR + INCREMENT 1/4 SPEED (motor frame, robot forward)", 0
sHold2Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 3 of 9 - LEFT MOTOR - INCREMENT 1/4 SPEED (motor frame, robot reverse)", 0
sHold3Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 4 of 9 - RIGHT MOTOR + INCREMENT 1/4 SPEED (motor frame, robot reverse)", 0
sHold4Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 5 of 9 - RIGHT MOTOR - INCREMENT 1/4 SPEED (motor frame, robot forward)", 0
sHold5Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 6 of 9 - LEFT MOTOR + INCREMENT 1/2 SPEED (motor frame, robot forward)", 0
sHold6Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 7 of 9 - LEFT MOTOR - INCREMENT 1/2 SPEED (motor frame, robot reverse)", 0
sHold7Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 8 of 9 - RIGHT MOTOR + INCREMENT 1/2 SPEED (motor frame, robot reverse)", 0
sHold8Caption   BYTE    "HOLD 9 of 9 - RIGHT MOTOR - INCREMENT 1/2 SPEED (motor frame, robot forward)", 0

VAR { run-wide state }

    LONG    bRunReturned                                    ' TRUE once runSession() reached its end
    LONG    bPreflightOk                                    ' TRUE when both wheels turned in preflight
    LONG    holdsRun                                        ' holds measured so far

VAR { overflow-proof running means, index ACC_* }

    LONG    accMean[ACC_SLOTS]                              ' floor(sum / count)
    LONG    accRem[ACC_SLOTS]                               ' sum - accMean * count, 0 <= rem < count
    LONG    accCount[ACC_SLOTS]                             ' samples added
    LONG    accMin[ACC_SLOTS]                               ' smallest clamped sample
    LONG    accMax[ACC_SLOTS]                               ' largest clamped sample

VAR { per-hold results, index HOLD_* -- the seam a later sign-off emitter reads }

    LONG    holdResultCode[HOLD_COUNT]                      ' RES_*
    LONG    holdIncre[HOLD_COUNT]                           ' signed motor increment commanded
    LONG    bHoldStarted[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' TRUE when start() gave a cog that reported ready
    LONG    holdStartCog[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' start()'s return
    LONG    holdSenseCog[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' startSenseCog()'s return
    LONG    holdBoardRev[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' REV_* recorded at start
    LONG    holdDeadGap[HOLD_COUNT]                         ' testGetDriveConstants() deadGap
    LONG    holdPwmLimit[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdDutyMin[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdDutyMax[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdAdcFrame[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdFrameCnt[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    bHoldAtSpeed[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' TRUE when DCS_AT_SPEED was seen
    LONG    holdSteadyMs[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' ms from command to AT_SPEED
    LONG    holdSteadySrc[HOLD_COUNT]                       ' pointer to RAMPED / TIMEOUT / ZEROCMD, 0 when not run
    LONG    holdSteadyRate[HOLD_COUNT]                      ' waitForSteady()'s hall-rate at its declaration
    LONG    bHoldStopped[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' TRUE when STOPPED was seen after the zero command
    LONG    holdZeroSamples[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdZeroX10[HOLD_COUNT]                         ' same-lifetime zero, mV x10
    LONG    holdSamples[HOLD_COUNT]                         ' window samples
    LONG    holdWinMs[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdRawX10[HOLD_COUNT]                          ' window sense mean, mV x10
    LONG    holdNetX10[HOLD_COUNT]                          ' raw minus the same-lifetime zero, mV x10
    LONG    holdMinMv[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdMaxMv[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdAmpsMean[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' getCurrent() amps x 10_000, window mean
    LONG    holdWattsMean[HOLD_COUNT]                       ' getCurrent() mW, window mean
    LONG    bHoldMotionValid[HOLD_COUNT]                    ' TRUE when the window ran and the cog was up at its end
    LONG    holdRpm[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdTicks[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdRateX10[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdNegDeg[HOLD_COUNT]                          ' testGetFwdRevIndep() fwd (negative increments)
    LONG    holdPosDeg[HOLD_COUNT]                          ' testGetFwdRevIndep() rev (positive increments)
    LONG    holdDutyMean[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    holdErrMean[HOLD_COUNT]
    LONG    bHoldIntegValid[HOLD_COUNT]                     ' TRUE when the counts were read from a running cog
    LONG    holdMissed[HOLD_COUNT]                          ' hall missed transitions since this hold's start
    LONG    holdIllegal[HOLD_COUNT]                         ' illegal hall codes since this hold's start
    LONG    holdDrvState[HOLD_COUNT]                        ' DCS_* after the stop wait

PUB main() | trapCode
'' Run the unattended characterisation: banner, preflight, every hold, then stop both wheels and
'' end the session. This is the one exit path.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local trapCode - value delivered by the abort trap around runSession()

    initRun()
    emitBanner()
    emitPlan()
    bRunReturned := FALSE
    trapCode := \runSession()                               ' a library abort lands here, not past the stop()s
    shutdownMotors()                                        ' EVERY path: both wheels stop()
    emitEnd(trapCode)
    debug("* BENCH CHAR RUN COMPLETE -- safe to disconnect")
    ' QUOTED, not backticked -- a backtick makes it a display command and the marker is missed.
    debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")

PRI initRun() | holdIdx
' Reset run-wide state and mark every hold not run.
'
' @local holdIdx - HOLD_* index

    bRunReturned := FALSE
    bPreflightOk := FALSE
    holdsRun := 0
    repeat holdIdx from HOLD_ZERO to HOLD_COUNT - 1
        clearHold(holdIdx)
        holdResultCode[holdIdx] := RES_NOT_RUN

PRI runSession() : bCompleted
' Preflight, then every configured hold. A preflight miss skips the holds.
'
' @returns bCompleted - TRUE when every configured hold ran

    bCompleted := FALSE
    bPreflightOk := preflightWheels()
    if bPreflightOk
        runAllHolds()
        bCompleted := TRUE
    else
        debug("! SKIPPING HOLDS -- see BC-PREFLIGHT above. Fix the wiring or the declared pin group,")
        debug("!   then re-run. Running nine holds against a wheel that cannot turn wastes the session.")
    bRunReturned := TRUE

PRI preflightWheels() : bOk | side, startedCog, bReady, ticksBefore, ticksAfter, ticksMoved, bStopped
' Prove each declared wheel can actually turn before committing the session to nine holds.
' Motion, not getBoardType(), is the check: detection is under investigation this sprint. On
' 2026-09-11 the bench config named a pin group with no board on it, and nine holds ran on it.
'
' @returns bOk - TRUE when both declared wheels moved
'
' @local side - SIDE_LEFT then SIDE_RIGHT
' @local startedCog - start()'s return
' @local bReady - TRUE when the driver reported ready
' @local ticksBefore - hall ticks before the nudge
' @local ticksAfter - hall ticks after the nudge
' @local ticksMoved - signed tick delta across the nudge
' @local bStopped - TRUE when STOPPED was seen after the nudge

    bOk := TRUE
    repeat side from SIDE_LEFT to SIDE_RIGHT
        ticksMoved := 0
        bStopped := FALSE
        startedCog, bReady := startSide(side)
        if bReady
            ticksBefore := wheelTicks(side)
            commandMotor(side, PREFLIGHT_INCRE)
            waitms(PREFLIGHT_MS)
            ticksAfter := wheelTicks(side)
            commandMotor(side, 0)
            bStopped := waitStoppedFor(side)
            ticksMoved := ticksAfter - ticksBefore
        shutdownMotors()
        emitPreflight(side, startedCog, ticksMoved, bStopped)
        if ticksMoved == 0
            bOk := FALSE
            debug("!  wheel on that pin group did NOT turn -- wrong pin group, or wiring, or a dead board")

PRI runAllHolds() | holdIdx
' Run every configured hold in sequence, quiescent zero through HOLD_LAST, printing each after
' its wheel has stopped.
'
' @local holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier of the hold currently running

    repeat holdIdx from HOLD_ZERO to HOLD_LAST
        measureHold(holdIdx)
        holdsRun += 1
        emitHoldRecords(holdIdx)

PRI holdInfo(holdIdx) : side, sign, speedIncre, pCaption, pRobotTok, pRungTok
' Return the fixed description of one hold -- the single source of truth for the sequence.
' Motor frame throughout: LEFT + increment is robot forward, RIGHT + increment is robot reverse.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier to describe
' @returns side - SIDE_* the hold drives
' @returns sign - +1 positive increment, -1 negative increment, 0 for the quiescent hold
' @returns speedIncre - unsigned motor-increment magnitude for this hold's rung
' @returns pCaption - pointer to this hold's caption text
' @returns pRobotTok - pointer to the robot-frame direction token (FWD / REV / NONE)
' @returns pRungTok - pointer to this hold's speed-rung token

    case holdIdx
        HOLD_ZERO:
            side := HOLD_ZERO_SIDE
            sign := 0
            speedIncre := 0
            pCaption := @sHold0Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotNone
            pRungTok := @sRungZero
        HOLD_L_FWD_QTR:
            side := SIDE_LEFT
            sign := 1
            speedIncre := QTR_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold1Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotFwd
            pRungTok := @sRungQtr
        HOLD_L_REV_QTR:
            side := SIDE_LEFT
            sign := -1
            speedIncre := QTR_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold2Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotRev
            pRungTok := @sRungQtr
        HOLD_R_FWD_QTR:
            side := SIDE_RIGHT
            sign := 1
            speedIncre := QTR_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold3Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotRev
            pRungTok := @sRungQtr
        HOLD_R_REV_QTR:
            side := SIDE_RIGHT
            sign := -1
            speedIncre := QTR_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold4Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotFwd
            pRungTok := @sRungQtr
        HOLD_L_FWD_HALF:
            side := SIDE_LEFT
            sign := 1
            speedIncre := HALF_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold5Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotFwd
            pRungTok := @sRungHalf
        HOLD_L_REV_HALF:
            side := SIDE_LEFT
            sign := -1
            speedIncre := HALF_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold6Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotRev
            pRungTok := @sRungHalf
        HOLD_R_FWD_HALF:
            side := SIDE_RIGHT
            sign := 1
            speedIncre := HALF_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold7Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotRev
            pRungTok := @sRungHalf
        other:                                               ' HOLD_R_REV_HALF
            side := SIDE_RIGHT
            sign := -1
            speedIncre := HALF_SPEED_INCRE
            pCaption := @sHold8Caption
            pRobotTok := @sRobotFwd
            pRungTok := @sRungHalf

PRI measureHold(holdIdx) | side, sign, speedIncre, motorIncre, bWindowGo, steadyTok, steadyMs, steadyRate
' Measure one hold end to end into the per-hold VAR longs; prints nothing. Steps: start the
' hold's wheel with the other wheel not running, same-lifetime zero, command, AT_SPEED, rate
' check, settle, window, zero command, stop wait, read integrity counts, stop the wheel.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* identifier of the hold to measure
'
' @local side - SIDE_* the hold drives
' @local sign - +1, -1, or 0 for the quiescent hold
' @local speedIncre - unsigned increment magnitude
' @local motorIncre - signed increment commanded (sign * speedIncre)
' @local bWindowGo - TRUE when the sample window may run
' @local steadyTok - waitForSteady()'s source token
' @local steadyMs - waitForSteady()'s elapsed ms (not recorded; AT_SPEED time is)
' @local steadyRate - waitForSteady()'s hall rate at its declaration

    side, sign, speedIncre, _, _, _ := holdInfo(holdIdx)
    clearHold(holdIdx)
    motorIncre := sign * speedIncre
    holdIncre[holdIdx] := motorIncre
    bWindowGo := FALSE
    startHoldWheel(holdIdx, side)
    if bHoldStarted[holdIdx]
        measureZero(holdIdx, side)
        if motorIncre == 0
            steadyTok, steadyMs, steadyRate := waitForSteady(side, 0)
            holdSteadySrc[holdIdx] := steadyTok
            holdSteadyRate[holdIdx] := steadyRate
            bWindowGo := (holdResultCode[holdIdx] == RES_OK)
        elseif holdResultCode[holdIdx] == RES_OK
            commandMotor(side, motorIncre)
            if waitAtSpeed(holdIdx, side)
                steadyTok, steadyMs, steadyRate := waitForSteady(side, motorIncre)
                holdSteadySrc[holdIdx] := steadyTok
                holdSteadyRate[holdIdx] := steadyRate
                ' a rate-check timeout is recorded as steady_src TIMEOUT, never as the hold's result:
                '  AT_SPEED (the driver's own ramp-complete state) has already been seen, and at
                '  quarter speed one STEADY_SAMPLE_MS sample is ~25 ticks, so +/-1 tick of
                '  quantisation is already 4% against STEADY_TOL_PCT 5 -- the hold is measured either way
                bWindowGo := settleHold(holdIdx, side)
        if bWindowGo
            sampleWindow(holdIdx, side)
        if wheelCogUp(side)
            commandMotor(side, 0)
            bHoldStopped[holdIdx] := waitStoppedFor(side)
            if bHoldStopped[holdIdx] == FALSE
                setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_STOP_TIMEOUT)
        if wheelCogUp(side)
            holdMissed[holdIdx], holdIllegal[holdIdx] := wheelIntegrity(side)
            bHoldIntegValid[holdIdx] := TRUE
            holdDrvState[holdIdx] := wheelDrvState(side)
    shutdownMotors()

PRI clearHold(holdIdx)
' Reset one hold's record to its not-measured state, result OK.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index

    holdResultCode[holdIdx] := RES_OK
    holdIncre[holdIdx] := 0
    bHoldStarted[holdIdx] := FALSE
    holdStartCog[holdIdx] := -1
    holdSenseCog[holdIdx] := -1
    holdBoardRev[holdIdx] := wheelL.REV_Unknown
    holdDeadGap[holdIdx] := 0
    holdPwmLimit[holdIdx] := 0
    holdDutyMin[holdIdx] := 0
    holdDutyMax[holdIdx] := 0
    holdAdcFrame[holdIdx] := 0
    holdFrameCnt[holdIdx] := 0
    bHoldAtSpeed[holdIdx] := FALSE
    holdSteadyMs[holdIdx] := 0
    holdSteadySrc[holdIdx] := 0
    holdSteadyRate[holdIdx] := 0
    bHoldStopped[holdIdx] := FALSE
    holdZeroSamples[holdIdx] := 0
    holdZeroX10[holdIdx] := 0
    holdSamples[holdIdx] := 0
    holdWinMs[holdIdx] := 0
    holdRawX10[holdIdx] := 0
    holdNetX10[holdIdx] := 0
    holdMinMv[holdIdx] := 0
    holdMaxMv[holdIdx] := 0
    holdAmpsMean[holdIdx] := 0
    holdWattsMean[holdIdx] := 0
    bHoldMotionValid[holdIdx] := FALSE
    holdRpm[holdIdx] := 0
    holdTicks[holdIdx] := 0
    holdRateX10[holdIdx] := 0
    holdNegDeg[holdIdx] := 0
    holdPosDeg[holdIdx] := 0
    holdDutyMean[holdIdx] := 0
    holdErrMean[holdIdx] := 0
    bHoldIntegValid[holdIdx] := FALSE
    holdMissed[holdIdx] := 0
    holdIllegal[holdIdx] := 0
    holdDrvState[holdIdx] := wheelL.DCS_Unknown

PRI setHoldResult(holdIdx, resCode)
' Record a hold result: the first cause is kept, but a fault or a lost cog always overwrites,
' because either one invalidates whatever timeout came before it.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
' @param resCode - RES_* cause

    if (holdResultCode[holdIdx] == RES_OK) or (resCode == RES_FAULT) or (resCode == RES_NO_COG)
        holdResultCode[holdIdx] := resCode

PRI startHoldWheel(holdIdx, side) | startedCog, bReady
' Start the hold's wheel with the other wheel not running, start its sense task, and record the
' start-time readings: start() return, detected board revision and the drive constants.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
'
' @local startedCog - start()'s return
' @local bReady - TRUE when the driver reported ready

    startedCog, bReady := startSide(side)
    holdStartCog[holdIdx] := startedCog
    if (startedCog < 0) or (startedCog > MAX_COG_ID)
        setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_NO_COG)
    elseif bReady == FALSE
        setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_READY_TIMEOUT)
    else
        bHoldStarted[holdIdx] := TRUE
        holdSenseCog[holdIdx] := wheelStartSense(side)      ' rpm is maintained only by this task
        holdBoardRev[holdIdx] := wheelBoardRev(side)
        holdDeadGap[holdIdx], holdPwmLimit[holdIdx], holdDutyMin[holdIdx], holdDutyMax[holdIdx], ...
            holdAdcFrame[holdIdx], holdFrameCnt[holdIdx] := wheelDriveConstants(side)

PRI startSide(side) : startedCog, bReady
' Stop both wheels, then start only the named wheel and wait (bounded) for it to report ready.
' stop() on a never-started instance touches no pin (isp_bldc_motor stop() guards its pinclear
' on this instance's own pin claim).
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns startedCog - start()'s return: cog id 0..7, or -1
' @returns bReady - TRUE when the started driver reported ready within READY_TIMEOUT_MS

    shutdownMotors()
    startedCog := -1
    bReady := FALSE
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        startedCog := wheelR.start(RIGHT_TEST_BASE, TEST_VOLTAGE, TEST_DET_MODE)
    else
        startedCog := wheelL.start(LEFT_TEST_BASE, TEST_VOLTAGE, TEST_DET_MODE)
    if startedCog >= 0
        bReady := waitUntilReady(side)

PRI waitUntilReady(side) : bReady | startMs
' Wait, bounded by READY_TIMEOUT_MS, for the just-started driver cog to report ready.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bReady - TRUE when ready was seen
'
' @local startMs - getms() when the wait began

    bReady := FALSE
    startMs := getms()
    repeat
        if wheelIsReady(side)
            bReady := TRUE
            quit
        if (getms() - startMs) >= READY_TIMEOUT_MS
            quit
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)

PRI measureZero(holdIdx, side) | sampleIdx, nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, bDidFault
' Read the current-sense zero at zero command, in this hold's own driver lifetime (PL-32).
' No debug() and no debug-emitting library call inside this loop.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
'
' @local sampleIdx - sample counter
' @local nDuty - duty sample (unused here)
' @local nErr - error sample (unused here)
' @local nSenseI - sense_i_mV sample
' @local eDrvrState - DCS_* sample
' @local bDidFault - fault sample

    accReset(ACC_ZERO)
    repeat sampleIdx from 1 to ZERO_SAMPLES
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)
        if wheelCogUp(side) == FALSE
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_NO_COG)
            quit
        nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelTelemetry(side)
        if bDidFault or (eDrvrState == wheelL.DCS_FAULTED)
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_FAULT)
            quit
        accAdd(ACC_ZERO, nSenseI)
    holdZeroSamples[holdIdx] := accCount[ACC_ZERO]
    holdZeroX10[holdIdx] := accMeanX10(ACC_ZERO)

PRI waitAtSpeed(holdIdx, side) : bAtSpeed | startMs, eDrvrState, bDidFault, nDuty, nErr, nSenseI
' Wait, bounded by ATSPEED_TIMEOUT_MS, for DCS_AT_SPEED after a motion command.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bAtSpeed - TRUE when AT_SPEED was seen
'
' @local startMs - getms() at the wait start
' @local eDrvrState - DCS_* sample
' @local bDidFault - fault sample
' @local nDuty - duty sample (unused here)
' @local nErr - error sample (unused here)
' @local nSenseI - sense sample (unused here)

    bAtSpeed := FALSE
    startMs := getms()
    repeat
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)
        if wheelCogUp(side) == FALSE
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_NO_COG)
            quit
        nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelTelemetry(side)
        if bDidFault or (eDrvrState == wheelL.DCS_FAULTED)
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_FAULT)
            quit
        if eDrvrState == wheelL.DCS_AT_SPEED
            bAtSpeed := TRUE
            quit
        if (getms() - startMs) >= ATSPEED_TIMEOUT_MS
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_STEADY_TIMEOUT)
            quit
    holdSteadyMs[holdIdx] := getms() - startMs
    bHoldAtSpeed[holdIdx] := bAtSpeed

PRI settleHold(holdIdx, side) : bSettled | startMs, eDrvrState, bDidFault, nDuty, nErr, nSenseI
' Hold SETTLE_MS at the commanded increment, polling for a fault or a lost cog.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bSettled - TRUE when the settle completed without a fault or lost cog
'
' @local startMs - getms() at settle start
' @local eDrvrState - DCS_* sample
' @local bDidFault - fault sample
' @local nDuty - duty sample (unused here)
' @local nErr - error sample (unused here)
' @local nSenseI - sense sample (unused here)

    bSettled := TRUE
    startMs := getms()
    repeat
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)
        if wheelCogUp(side) == FALSE
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_NO_COG)
            bSettled := FALSE
            quit
        nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelTelemetry(side)
        if bDidFault or (eDrvrState == wheelL.DCS_FAULTED)
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_FAULT)
            bSettled := FALSE
            quit
        if (getms() - startMs) >= SETTLE_MS
            quit

PRI sampleWindow(holdIdx, side) | startMs, startTicks, endTicks, nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, ...
    bDidFault, nAmps, nWatts, rateTicks
' Sample every SAMPLE_MS for WINDOW_MS into the running means, then fill the hold's window
' fields. testGetRpm() is read at the window's end: at least SETTLE_MS + WINDOW_MS after
' AT_SPEED, past the ~1 s the sense task's rpm window needs. No debug() inside the loop, and
' every library call in it (testGetMotorCog, testGetTelemetry, getCurrent) emits none.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
'
' @local startMs - getms() at window start
' @local startTicks - hall ticks at window start
' @local endTicks - hall ticks at window end
' @local nDuty - duty sample
' @local nErr - position-error sample
' @local nSenseI - sense_i_mV sample
' @local eDrvrState - DCS_* sample
' @local bDidFault - fault sample
' @local nAmps - getCurrent() amps x 10_000 sample
' @local nWatts - getCurrent() mW sample
' @local rateTicks - tick count clamped for the rate arithmetic

    accReset(ACC_SENSE)
    accReset(ACC_AMPS)
    accReset(ACC_WATTS)
    accReset(ACC_DUTY)
    accReset(ACC_ERR)
    startTicks := wheelTicks(side)
    startMs := getms()
    repeat
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)
        if wheelCogUp(side) == FALSE
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_NO_COG)
            quit
        nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelTelemetry(side)
        if bDidFault or (eDrvrState == wheelL.DCS_FAULTED)
            setHoldResult(holdIdx, RES_FAULT)
            quit
        nAmps, nWatts := wheelCurrent(side)
        accAdd(ACC_SENSE, nSenseI)
        accAdd(ACC_AMPS, nAmps)
        accAdd(ACC_WATTS, nWatts)
        accAdd(ACC_DUTY, nDuty)
        accAdd(ACC_ERR, nErr)
        if (getms() - startMs) >= WINDOW_MS
            quit
    holdWinMs[holdIdx] := getms() - startMs
    holdSamples[holdIdx] := accCount[ACC_SENSE]
    if accCount[ACC_SENSE] > 0
        holdRawX10[holdIdx] := accMeanX10(ACC_SENSE)
        holdMinMv[holdIdx] := accMin[ACC_SENSE]
        holdMaxMv[holdIdx] := accMax[ACC_SENSE]
        holdAmpsMean[holdIdx] := accMean[ACC_AMPS]
        holdWattsMean[holdIdx] := accMean[ACC_WATTS]
        holdDutyMean[holdIdx] := accMean[ACC_DUTY]
        holdErrMean[holdIdx] := accMean[ACC_ERR]
        ' both operands are clamped to LIM_BIG first, so the difference is within +/-2e9 < POSX
        holdNetX10[holdIdx] := ((holdRawX10[holdIdx] #> -LIM_BIG) <# LIM_BIG) - ((holdZeroX10[holdIdx] #> -LIM_BIG) <# LIM_BIG)
        if wheelCogUp(side)
            endTicks := wheelTicks(side)
            holdTicks[holdIdx] := abs(endTicks - startTicks)
            rateTicks := holdTicks[holdIdx] <# RATE_TICKS_CAP
            if holdWinMs[holdIdx] > 0
                holdRateX10[holdIdx] := (rateTicks * RATE_X10_SCALE) / holdWinMs[holdIdx]
            holdRpm[holdIdx] := wheelRpm(side)
            holdNegDeg[holdIdx], holdPosDeg[holdIdx] := wheelOffsets(side)
            bHoldMotionValid[holdIdx] := TRUE

PRI waitStoppedFor(side) : bStopped | startMs
' Wait, bounded by STOP_TIMEOUT_MS, for the named wheel's running driver to report STOPPED.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bStopped - TRUE when STOPPED was seen
'
' @local startMs - getms() when the wait began

    bStopped := FALSE
    startMs := getms()
    repeat
        if wheelCogUp(side) == FALSE
            quit
        if wheelIsStopped(side)
            bStopped := TRUE
            quit
        if (getms() - startMs) >= STOP_TIMEOUT_MS
            quit
        waitms(SAMPLE_MS)

PRI waitForSteady(side, cmdIncre) : steadySrcTok, elapsedMs, tickRate | prevPos, curPos, ...
    prevRate, curRate, consecCount, bTimedOut, diffPct
' Declare steady state either instantly (the quiescent-zero hold, ZEROCMD) or once
' STEADY_CONFIRM_SAMPLES consecutive hall-tick-rate samples agree within STEADY_TOL_PCT, or
' at STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS regardless (declare steady anyway, source TIMEOUT).
'
' @param side - SIDE_* under test
' @param cmdIncre - signed motor increment just commanded; 0 selects the ZEROCMD path
' @returns steadySrcTok - pointer to RAMPED / TIMEOUT / ZEROCMD
' @returns elapsedMs - milliseconds from command issue to this steady-state declaration
' @returns tickRate - hall-tick rate observed at the declaration (0 for ZEROCMD)
'
' @local prevPos - hall-tick position at the previous sample
' @local curPos - hall-tick position at the current sample
' @local prevRate - hall-tick rate at the previous sample, -1 before the first sample
' @local curRate - hall-tick rate at the current sample
' @local consecCount - consecutive samples agreeing within STEADY_TOL_PCT
' @local bTimedOut - TRUE once STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS has elapsed without confirmation
' @local diffPct - percent difference between curRate and prevRate

    if cmdIncre == 0
        steadySrcTok := @sSteadyZerocmd
        elapsedMs := 0
        tickRate := 0
    else
        prevPos := wheelTicks(side)
        prevRate := -1
        consecCount := 0
        elapsedMs := 0
        bTimedOut := FALSE
        repeat
            waitms(STEADY_SAMPLE_MS)
            elapsedMs += STEADY_SAMPLE_MS
            curPos := wheelTicks(side)
            curRate := absValue(curPos - prevPos) * (MS_PER_SEC / STEADY_SAMPLE_MS)
            prevPos := curPos
            if prevRate == -1
                consecCount := 1
            elseif prevRate == 0
                consecCount := (curRate == 0) ? consecCount + 1 : 1
            else
                diffPct := (absValue(curRate - prevRate) * 100) / prevRate
                consecCount := (diffPct <= STEADY_TOL_PCT) ? consecCount + 1 : 1
            prevRate := curRate
            bTimedOut := (elapsedMs >= STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS)
        until (consecCount >= STEADY_CONFIRM_SAMPLES) or bTimedOut
        tickRate := curRate
        steadySrcTok := bTimedOut ? @sSteadyTimeout : @sSteadyRamped

PRI absValue(signedVal) : magnitude
' Return the absolute value of a signed number.
'
' @param signedVal - value to make non-negative
' @returns magnitude - |signedVal|

    magnitude := (signedVal < 0) ? (0 - signedVal) : signedVal

PRI accReset(accIdx)
' Empty one running mean.
'
' @param accIdx - ACC_* slot

    accMean[accIdx] := 0
    accRem[accIdx] := 0
    accCount[accIdx] := 0
    accMin[accIdx] := POSX
    accMax[accIdx] := NEGX

PRI accAdd(accIdx, sampleVal) | clampedVal, newCount, deltaVal, quotVal, remVal
' Add one sample to a running mean without ever storing the sum (PL-20; bound in the CON block
' above). Floor division is built from truncating / by correcting a negative remainder, so the
' result does not depend on whether / truncates or floors.
'
' @param accIdx - ACC_* slot
' @param sampleVal - the sample
'
' @local clampedVal - sample clamped to +/-ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT
' @local newCount - count including this sample
' @local deltaVal - remainder + sample - mean, |deltaVal| < 1_100_000_000
' @local quotVal - deltaVal / newCount, corrected to a floor
' @local remVal - deltaVal - quotVal * newCount, corrected into 0..newCount-1

    clampedVal := (sampleVal #> (0 - ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT)) <# ACC_SAMPLE_LIMIT
    if accCount[accIdx] < ACC_COUNT_CAP
        newCount := accCount[accIdx] + 1
        deltaVal := accRem[accIdx] + clampedVal - accMean[accIdx]
        quotVal := deltaVal / newCount
        remVal := deltaVal - (quotVal * newCount)
        if remVal < 0
            remVal += newCount
            quotVal -= 1
        accMean[accIdx] += quotVal
        accRem[accIdx] := remVal
        accCount[accIdx] := newCount
        accMin[accIdx] := accMin[accIdx] <# clampedVal
        accMax[accIdx] := accMax[accIdx] #> clampedVal

PRI accMeanX10(accIdx) : meanX10 | boundedMean
' Return a running mean x10, truncated toward negative infinity; 0 when empty.
'
' @param accIdx - ACC_* slot
' @returns meanX10 - mean x10
'
' @local boundedMean - floor mean clamped to +/-ACC_MEAN_X10_LIMIT so the x10 cannot overflow

    meanX10 := 0
    if accCount[accIdx] > 0
        boundedMean := (accMean[accIdx] #> (0 - ACC_MEAN_X10_LIMIT)) <# ACC_MEAN_X10_LIMIT
        meanX10 := (boundedMean * X10) + ((accRem[accIdx] * X10) / accCount[accIdx])

PRI commandMotor(side, motorIncre) | safeIncre
' Command a signed motor increment -- the TESTING USE raw-increment path, never followed by
' stopAfterTime(). Anything beyond DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE is commanded as zero.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @param motorIncre - signed motor increment to drive at
'
' @local safeIncre - increment actually commanded

    safeIncre := motorIncre
    if abs(motorIncre) > DRIVE_CEILING_INCRE
        safeIncre := 0
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        wheelR.testDriveAtMotorIncrement(safeIncre)
    elseif side == SIDE_LEFT
        wheelL.testDriveAtMotorIncrement(safeIncre)

PRI shutdownMotors()
' Stop both wheels unconditionally. stop() on a never-started instance touches no pin.

    wheelL.stop()
    wheelR.stop()

PRI wheelCogUp(side) : bRunning
' Report whether the named wheel has a running driver cog (stop() zeroes motorCog).
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bRunning - TRUE when the driver cog is running

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        bRunning := (wheelR.testGetMotorCog() <> 0)
    else
        bRunning := (wheelL.testGetMotorCog() <> 0)

PRI wheelIsReady(side) : bReady
' Report whether the named wheel's running driver reports ready.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bReady - TRUE when running and ready

    bReady := FALSE
    if wheelCogUp(side)
        if side == SIDE_RIGHT
            bReady := wheelR.isReady()
        else
            bReady := wheelL.isReady()

PRI wheelIsStopped(side) : bStopped
' Report whether the named wheel's running driver reports STOPPED.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns bStopped - TRUE when running and STOPPED

    bStopped := FALSE
    if wheelCogUp(side)
        if side == SIDE_RIGHT
            bStopped := wheelR.isStopped()
        else
            bStopped := wheelL.isStopped()

PRI wheelDrvState(side) : eDrvrState
' Driver state of the named wheel, DCS_Unknown when no cog is running.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns eDrvrState - DCS_* state

    eDrvrState := wheelL.DCS_Unknown
    if wheelCogUp(side)
        if side == SIDE_RIGHT
            eDrvrState := wheelR.getDriverState()
        else
            eDrvrState := wheelL.getDriverState()

PRI wheelTelemetry(side) : nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, eDrvrState, bDidFault
' Snapshot the named wheel's per-cycle driver status. Callers check wheelCogUp() first (PL-21).
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns nDuty - latest duty value
' @returns nErr - latest position-error value
' @returns nSenseI - latest sense_i_mV, true millivolts
' @returns eDrvrState - DCS_* driver state
' @returns bDidFault - TRUE when the driver has faulted

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, _, _, _, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelR.testGetTelemetry()
    else
        nDuty, nErr, nSenseI, _, _, _, eDrvrState, bDidFault := wheelL.testGetTelemetry()

PRI wheelCurrent(side) : nAmps, nWatts
' getCurrent() of the named wheel: amps x 10_000 (0.1 mA units) and mW, per its doc comment.
' Watts use the nominal TEST_VOLTAGE, not a measured pack voltage.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns nAmps - current, 0.1 mA units
' @returns nWatts - power, mW

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        nAmps, nWatts := wheelR.getCurrent()
    else
        nAmps, nWatts := wheelL.getCurrent()

PRI wheelTicks(side) : nTicks
' Raw hall ticks of the named wheel.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns nTicks - hall-tick position

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        nTicks := wheelR.getRawHallTicks()
    else
        nTicks := wheelL.getRawHallTicks()

PRI wheelIntegrity(side) : nMissed, nIllegal
' Hall integrity counts of the named wheel since its last start.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns nMissed - missed transitions
' @returns nIllegal - illegal hall codes

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        nMissed, nIllegal := wheelR.getHallIntegrityCounts()
    else
        nMissed, nIllegal := wheelL.getHallIntegrityCounts()

PRI wheelOffsets(side) : negDeg, posDeg
' Applied commutation offsets of the named wheel.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns negDeg - offset_fwd degrees (negative increments)
' @returns posDeg - offset_rev degrees (positive increments)

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        negDeg, posDeg := wheelR.testGetFwdRevIndep()
    else
        negDeg, posDeg := wheelL.testGetFwdRevIndep()

PRI wheelRpm(side) : nRpm
' testGetRpm() of the named wheel (maintained only by its sense task).
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns nRpm - rpm over the sense task's ~1 s window

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        nRpm := wheelR.testGetRpm()
    else
        nRpm := wheelL.testGetRpm()

PRI wheelStartSense(side) : senseCog
' startSenseCog() for the named wheel.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns senseCog - the sense task's cog id 0..7, or -1

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        senseCog := wheelR.startSenseCog()
    else
        senseCog := wheelL.startSenseCog()

PRI wheelBoardRev(side) : eBoardRev
' Board revision of the named wheel; with its driver running this is the revision recorded at start.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns eBoardRev - REV_* value

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        eBoardRev := wheelR.getBoardType()
    else
        eBoardRev := wheelL.getBoardType()

PRI wheelDriveConstants(side) : deadGap, pwmLimit, dutyMin, dutyMax, adcFrame, frameCnt
' testGetDriveConstants() of the named wheel.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @returns deadGap - commutation dead-time, system ticks
' @returns pwmLimit - PWM duty hard limit
' @returns dutyMin - minimum duty, 1/16ths
' @returns dutyMax - maximum duty, 1/16ths
' @returns adcFrame - ADC sample period
' @returns frameCnt - PWM frame length, system ticks

    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        deadGap, pwmLimit, dutyMin, dutyMax, adcFrame, frameCnt := wheelR.testGetDriveConstants()
    else
        deadGap, pwmLimit, dutyMin, dutyMax, adcFrame, frameCnt := wheelL.testGetDriveConstants()

PRI emitBanner()
' Emit BC-BANNER once. cfg_id is sourced from its own #ifdef, never a runtime test -- pnut-ts
' silently ignores an unknown -D, so a mistyped flag lands on the honest #else token. The pin
' bases, voltage and detect mode are stated outright so a log is attributable to hardware on its
' own evidence.
' Worst case: tag(9) + src_rev(16) + fmt(12) + cfg_id(13) + frame(12) + clkfreq(21) +
' left_base(15) + right_base(16) + voltage_enum(18) + det_mode(14) + hold_last(15) +
' qtr_incre(23) + half_incre(24) = 208 bytes.

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-BANNER")
    boundedField(@"src_rev", SRC_REV, LIM_SMALL)
    boundedField(@"fmt", FMT_VERSION, LIM_SMALL)
#ifdef BENCH_CFG
    tokenField(@"cfg_id", @sCfgBench, TOKMAX_CFG)
#else
    tokenField(@"cfg_id", @sCfgUser, TOKMAX_CFG)
#endif
    tokenField(@"frame", @sFrameMotor, TOKMAX_FRAME)
    boundedField(@"clkfreq", CLKFREQ, LIM_BIG)
    boundedField(@"left_base", LEFT_TEST_BASE, LIM_TINY)
    boundedField(@"right_base", RIGHT_TEST_BASE, LIM_TINY)
    boundedField(@"voltage_enum", TEST_VOLTAGE, LIM_TINY)
    boundedField(@"det_mode", TEST_DET_MODE, LIM_TINY)
    boundedField(@"hold_last", HOLD_LAST, LIM_TINY)
    boundedField(@"qtr_incre", QTR_SPEED_INCRE, LIM_BIG)
    boundedField(@"half_incre", HALF_SPEED_INCRE, LIM_BIG)
    lineEmit()

    debug("* PANIC PROCEDURE IS PHYSICAL BATTERY DISCONNECT ONLY -- emergencyCutoff() self-cancels in about 250 ms (finding S-4)")

PRI emitPlan()
' Emit BC-PLAN once: every timing and wait bound the holds run under.
' Worst case: tag(7) + sample_ms(18) + zero_samples(21) + settle_ms(18) + window_ms(18) +
' ready_timeout_ms(25) + atspeed_timeout_ms(27) + steady_timeout_ms(26) + stop_timeout_ms(24) +
' hold0_motor(18) = 202 bytes.

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-PLAN")
    boundedField(@"sample_ms", SAMPLE_MS, LIM_SMALL)
    boundedField(@"zero_samples", ZERO_SAMPLES, LIM_SMALL)
    boundedField(@"settle_ms", SETTLE_MS, LIM_SMALL)
    boundedField(@"window_ms", WINDOW_MS, LIM_SMALL)
    boundedField(@"ready_timeout_ms", READY_TIMEOUT_MS, LIM_SMALL)
    boundedField(@"atspeed_timeout_ms", ATSPEED_TIMEOUT_MS, LIM_SMALL)
    boundedField(@"steady_timeout_ms", STEADY_TIMEOUT_MS, LIM_SMALL)
    boundedField(@"stop_timeout_ms", STOP_TIMEOUT_MS, LIM_SMALL)
    tokenField(@"hold0_motor", motorToken(HOLD_ZERO_SIDE), TOKMAX_MOTOR)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitPreflight(side, startedCog, ticksMoved, bStopped)
' Emit BC-PREFLIGHT for one wheel. The base is chosen with if/else, and ok prints TRUE/FALSE.
' Worst case: tag(12) + motor(12) + base(10) + cog(9) + ticks(17) + ok(9) + stopped(14) = 83 bytes.
'
' @param side - SIDE_LEFT or SIDE_RIGHT
' @param startedCog - start()'s return
' @param ticksMoved - signed tick delta across the nudge
' @param bStopped - TRUE when STOPPED was seen after the nudge

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-PREFLIGHT")
    tokenField(@"motor", motorToken(side), TOKMAX_MOTOR)
    if side == SIDE_RIGHT
        boundedField(@"base", RIGHT_TEST_BASE, LIM_TINY)
    else
        boundedField(@"base", LEFT_TEST_BASE, LIM_TINY)
    boundedField(@"cog", startedCog, LIM_TINY)
    boundedField(@"ticks", ticksMoved, LIM_MID)
    boolField(@"ok", (ticksMoved <> 0))
    boolField(@"stopped", bStopped)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitHoldRecords(holdIdx)
' Emit one hold's records from its VAR longs, after its wheel has stopped: BC-SHEET, BC-START,
' BC-HOLD, BC-SENSE, BC-MOTION.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index

    emitSheet(holdIdx)
    emitStart(holdIdx)
    emitHold(holdIdx)
    emitSense(holdIdx)
    emitMotion(holdIdx)

PRI emitSheet(holdIdx) | pCaption
' Emit BC-SHEET: the hold's row number and caption (the caption names the frame).
' Worst case: tag(8) + row(9) + name(1+4+1+96=102) = 119 bytes.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
'
' @local pCaption - pointer to the caption

    _, _, _, pCaption, _, _ := holdInfo(holdIdx)
    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-SHEET")
    boundedField(@"row", holdIdx + 1, LIM_TINY)
    tokenField(@"name", pCaption, TOKMAX_CAPTION)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitStart(holdIdx) | side, bStarted
' Emit BC-START: start() return, sense task cog, detected board revision and drive constants
' (dead_gap in system ticks). Everything after cog prints NA when the driver did not start ready.
' Worst case: tag(8) + hold(10) + motor(12) + cog(9) + sense_cog(15) + board_rev(15) +
' board_id(17) + dead_gap(17) + pwm_limit(21) + duty_min(20) + duty_max(20) + adc_frame(21) +
' frame_cnt(21) = 206 bytes.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
'
' @local side - SIDE_* of the hold
' @local bStarted - TRUE when the driver started and reported ready

    side, _, _, _, _, _ := holdInfo(holdIdx)
    bStarted := bHoldStarted[holdIdx]
    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-START")
    boundedField(@"hold", holdIdx, LIM_TINY)
    tokenField(@"motor", motorToken(side), TOKMAX_MOTOR)
    boundedField(@"cog", holdStartCog[holdIdx], LIM_TINY)
    naOrBoundedField(@"sense_cog", holdSenseCog[holdIdx], LIM_TINY, bStarted)
    naOrBoundedField(@"board_rev", holdBoardRev[holdIdx], LIM_TINY, bStarted)
    if bStarted
        tokenField(@"board_id", boardToken(holdBoardRev[holdIdx]), TOKMAX_BOARD)
    else
        lineTextField(@"board_id", @sNa)
    naOrBoundedField(@"dead_gap", holdDeadGap[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL, bStarted)
    naOrBoundedField(@"pwm_limit", holdPwmLimit[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bStarted)
    naOrBoundedField(@"duty_min", holdDutyMin[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bStarted)
    naOrBoundedField(@"duty_max", holdDutyMax[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bStarted)
    naOrBoundedField(@"adc_frame", holdAdcFrame[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bStarted)
    naOrBoundedField(@"frame_cnt", holdFrameCnt[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bStarted)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitHold(holdIdx) | side, pRobotTok, pRungTok
' Emit BC-HOLD: identity (signed increment, robot_dir, frame), result and wait outcomes.
' Worst case: tag(7) + hold(10) + motor(12) + incre(19) + robot_dir(15) + frame(12) + rung(10) +
' result(22) + at_speed(15) + steady_ms(18) + steady_src(19) + steady_rate(20) + stopped(14) =
' 193 bytes.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
'
' @local side - SIDE_* of the hold
' @local pRobotTok - robot-frame direction token
' @local pRungTok - speed-rung token

    side, _, _, _, pRobotTok, pRungTok := holdInfo(holdIdx)
    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-HOLD")
    boundedField(@"hold", holdIdx, LIM_TINY)
    tokenField(@"motor", motorToken(side), TOKMAX_MOTOR)
    boundedField(@"incre", holdIncre[holdIdx], LIM_BIG)
    tokenField(@"robot_dir", pRobotTok, TOKMAX_ROBOT)
    tokenField(@"frame", @sFrameMotor, TOKMAX_FRAME)
    tokenField(@"rung", pRungTok, TOKMAX_RUNG)
    tokenField(@"result", resultToken(holdResultCode[holdIdx]), TOKMAX_RESULT)
    if holdIncre[holdIdx] <> 0
        boolField(@"at_speed", bHoldAtSpeed[holdIdx])
    else
        lineTextField(@"at_speed", @sNa)                    ' hold 0 never commands motion
    naOrBoundedField(@"steady_ms", holdSteadyMs[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL, bHoldStarted[holdIdx] and (holdIncre[holdIdx] <> 0))
    if holdSteadySrc[holdIdx] <> 0
        tokenField(@"steady_src", holdSteadySrc[holdIdx], TOKMAX_STEADY)
    else
        lineTextField(@"steady_src", @sNa)
    naOrBoundedField(@"steady_rate", holdSteadyRate[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL, holdSteadySrc[holdIdx] <> 0)
    boolField(@"stopped", bHoldStopped[holdIdx])
    lineEmit()

PRI emitSense(holdIdx) | bWindow, bZero, bBoardKnown
' Emit BC-SENSE: the window's raw sense mean, the same-lifetime zero, their difference (net), the
' window min/max, and getCurrent()'s window means. Amps and watts print NA unless the board was
' detected as REV_A or REV_B: isp_bldc_motor.spin2 init() leaves rSenseForBoard at -1 otherwise,
' and getCurrent() then divides by it (PL-25).
' Worst case: tag(8) + hold(10) + samples(16) + win_ms(15) + zero_samples(21) + raw_mV_x10(24) +
' zero_mV_x10(25) + net_mV_x10(24) + min_mV(20) + max_mV(20) + amps_x10k(21) + watts_mW(20) =
' 224 bytes.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
'
' @local bWindow - TRUE when the window took at least one sample
' @local bZero - TRUE when the zero took at least one sample
' @local bBoardKnown - TRUE when the start-time board revision is REV_A or REV_B

    bWindow := (holdSamples[holdIdx] > 0)
    bZero := (holdZeroSamples[holdIdx] > 0)
    bBoardKnown := (holdBoardRev[holdIdx] == wheelL.REV_A) or (holdBoardRev[holdIdx] == wheelL.REV_B)
    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-SENSE")
    boundedField(@"hold", holdIdx, LIM_TINY)
    boundedField(@"samples", holdSamples[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL)
    naOrBoundedField(@"win_ms", holdWinMs[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL, bWindow)
    boundedField(@"zero_samples", holdZeroSamples[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL)
    naOrBoundedField(@"raw_mV_x10", holdRawX10[holdIdx], LIM_BIG, bWindow)
    naOrBoundedField(@"zero_mV_x10", holdZeroX10[holdIdx], LIM_BIG, bZero)
    naOrBoundedField(@"net_mV_x10", holdNetX10[holdIdx], LIM_BIG, bWindow and bZero)
    naOrBoundedField(@"min_mV", holdMinMv[holdIdx], LIM_BIG, bWindow)
    naOrBoundedField(@"max_mV", holdMaxMv[holdIdx], LIM_BIG, bWindow)
    naOrBoundedField(@"amps_x10k", holdAmpsMean[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bWindow and bBoardKnown)
    naOrBoundedField(@"watts_mW", holdWattsMean[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bWindow and bBoardKnown)
    lineEmit()

PRI emitMotion(holdIdx) | bMotion, bWindow
' Emit BC-MOTION: rpm, ticks and tick rate over the window, applied offsets, duty and err window
' means, hall integrity counts since this hold's start, and the driver state after the stop wait.
' Worst case: tag(9) + hold(10) + rpm(12) + ticks(17) + rate_x10(17) + neg_deg(13) + pos_deg(13) +
' duty_mean(21) + err_mean(20) + missed(18) + illegal(19) + drv_state(15) = 184 bytes.
'
' @param holdIdx - HOLD_* index
'
' @local bMotion - TRUE when the window ran and the cog was up at its end
' @local bWindow - TRUE when the window took at least one sample

    bMotion := bHoldMotionValid[holdIdx]
    bWindow := (holdSamples[holdIdx] > 0)
    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-MOTION")
    boundedField(@"hold", holdIdx, LIM_TINY)
    naOrBoundedField(@"rpm", holdRpm[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL, bMotion and (holdSenseCog[holdIdx] >= 0))
    naOrBoundedField(@"ticks", holdTicks[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bMotion)
    naOrBoundedField(@"rate_x10", holdRateX10[holdIdx], LIM_SMALL, bMotion)
    naOrBoundedField(@"neg_deg", holdNegDeg[holdIdx], LIM_TINY, bMotion)
    naOrBoundedField(@"pos_deg", holdPosDeg[holdIdx], LIM_TINY, bMotion)
    naOrBoundedField(@"duty_mean", holdDutyMean[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bWindow)
    naOrBoundedField(@"err_mean", holdErrMean[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bWindow)
    naOrBoundedField(@"missed", holdMissed[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bHoldIntegValid[holdIdx])
    naOrBoundedField(@"illegal", holdIllegal[holdIdx], LIM_MID, bHoldIntegValid[holdIdx])
    naOrBoundedField(@"drv_state", holdDrvState[holdIdx], LIM_TINY, bHoldIntegValid[holdIdx])
    lineEmit()

PRI emitEnd(trapCode)
' Emit BC-END, the last record before the end marker.
' Worst case: tag(6) + exit(14) + preflight_ok(19) + holds_run(15) + lib_abort(16) + trap(16) =
' 86 bytes.
'
' @param trapCode - value the abort trap delivered around runSession()

    lineReset()
    lineAddText(@"BC-END")
    if bRunReturned and bPreflightOk and (holdsRun == HOLD_LAST + 1)
        tokenField(@"exit", @sExitComplete, TOKMAX_EXIT)
    else
        tokenField(@"exit", @sExitAborted, TOKMAX_EXIT)
    boolField(@"preflight_ok", bPreflightOk)
    boundedField(@"holds_run", holdsRun, LIM_TINY)
    boolField(@"lib_abort", (bRunReturned == FALSE))
    naOrBoundedField(@"trap", trapCode, LIM_MID, (bRunReturned == FALSE))
    lineEmit()

PRI boundedField(pFieldName, numValue, limitAbs)
' Append a numeric field clamped to +/- limitAbs, so its printed width is bounded.
'
' @param pFieldName - pointer to the field name
' @param numValue - the field's value
' @param limitAbs - clamp magnitude (one of the LIM_* widths)

    lineField(pFieldName, (numValue #> (0 - limitAbs)) <# limitAbs)

PRI naOrBoundedField(pFieldName, numValue, limitAbs, bValid)
' Append a clamped numeric field, or the token NA when the value was not measured.
'
' @param pFieldName - pointer to the field name
' @param numValue - the field's value
' @param limitAbs - clamp magnitude (one of the LIM_* widths)
' @param bValid - TRUE when numValue is a measurement

    if bValid
        boundedField(pFieldName, numValue, limitAbs)
    else
        lineTextField(pFieldName, @sNa)

PRI boolField(pFieldName, bFlag)
' Append a boolean field as the token TRUE or FALSE, never a number (PL-23).
'
' @param pFieldName - pointer to the field name
' @param bFlag - the field's value; any non-zero prints TRUE

    if bFlag <> FALSE
        lineTextField(pFieldName, @sTrue)
    else
        lineTextField(pFieldName, @sFalse)

PRI tokenField(pFieldName, pToken, maxLen)
' Append a token field; a token longer than maxLen prints as "?" so the width stays bounded.
'
' @param pFieldName - pointer to the field name
' @param pToken - pointer to the token text
' @param maxLen - the longest token this field may print

    if tokenFits(pToken, maxLen)
        lineTextField(pFieldName, pToken)
    else
        lineTextField(pFieldName, @sBadTok)

PRI tokenFits(pToken, maxLen) : bFits | charIdx
' Report whether a zero-terminated token is at most maxLen bytes, reading no more than maxLen + 1.
'
' @param pToken - pointer to the token text
' @param maxLen - the longest acceptable token
' @returns bFits - TRUE when the terminator is found within maxLen bytes
'
' @local charIdx - index into the token

    bFits := FALSE
    repeat charIdx from 0 to maxLen
        if BYTE[pToken][charIdx] == 0
            bFits := TRUE
            quit

PRI motorToken(side) : pTok
' Motor token for a side.
'
' @param side - SIDE_* value
' @returns pTok - LEFT, RIGHT or NONE

    case side
        SIDE_LEFT:
            pTok := @sMotLeft
        SIDE_RIGHT:
            pTok := @sMotRight
        other:
            pTok := @sMotNone

PRI boardToken(eBoardRev) : pTok
' Board revision token.
'
' @param eBoardRev - REV_* value
' @returns pTok - REV_A, REV_B or UNKNOWN

    case eBoardRev
        wheelL.REV_A:
            pTok := @sBoardRevA
        wheelL.REV_B:
            pTok := @sBoardRevB
        other:
            pTok := @sBoardUnknown

PRI resultToken(resCode) : pTok
' Hold result token.
'
' @param resCode - RES_* value
' @returns pTok - result token

    case resCode
        RES_OK:
            pTok := @sResOk
        RES_NO_COG:
            pTok := @sResNoCog
        RES_READY_TIMEOUT:
            pTok := @sResReadyTo
        RES_STEADY_TIMEOUT:
            pTok := @sResSteadyTo
        RES_FAULT:
            pTok := @sResFault
        RES_STOP_TIMEOUT:
            pTok := @sResStopTo
        other:
            pTok := @sResNotRun

PRI lineReset()
' Begin a new record.

    lineLen := 0
    BYTE[@lineBuf][0] := 0

PRI lineAddChar(charByte)
' Append one character to the record under assembly, silently dropping anything past the
' buffer. Every record in this file is well under LINE_BUF_SIZE; truncation would show as a
' short line in the log rather than as memory corruption.
'
' @param charByte - the character to append

    if lineLen < LINE_BUF_SIZE - 1
        BYTE[@lineBuf][lineLen] := charByte
        lineLen += 1
        BYTE[@lineBuf][lineLen] := 0

PRI lineAddText(pText) | srcIdx
' Append a zero-terminated string to the record under assembly. The loop is bounded as well
' as terminated, so an unterminated source string cannot hang the run.
'
' @param pText - pointer to the text to append
'
' @local srcIdx - index into the source text

    repeat srcIdx from 0 to LINE_BUF_SIZE - 1
        if BYTE[pText][srcIdx] == 0
            quit
        lineAddChar(BYTE[pText][srcIdx])

PRI lineAddNum(numValue) | digitStack[MAX_DEC_DIGITS], digitCount, absMagnitude, digitIdx
' Append a signed decimal number with an underscore every three digits, matching udec_() and
' sdec_() elsewhere in this tree's bench logs.
'
' @param numValue - the value to append
'
' @local digitStack - decimal digits of numValue, least significant first
' @local digitCount - how many entries of digitStack are in use
' @local absMagnitude - magnitude of numValue, consumed by the extraction loop
' @local digitIdx - index into digitStack while emitting

    absMagnitude := numValue
    if numValue < 0
        lineAddChar("-")
        absMagnitude := -numValue

    digitCount := 0
    repeat
        digitStack[digitCount] := absMagnitude // DEC_RADIX
        absMagnitude /= DEC_RADIX
        digitCount += 1
    until (absMagnitude == 0) or (digitCount == MAX_DEC_DIGITS)

    repeat digitIdx from digitCount - 1 to 0
        lineAddChar("0" + digitStack[digitIdx])
        if (digitIdx > 0) and (digitIdx // DIGITS_PER_GROUP == 0)
            lineAddChar("_")

PRI lineField(pFieldName, numValue)
' Append one ",name,<number>" field to the record under assembly.
'
' @param pFieldName - pointer to the field name
' @param numValue - the field's value

    lineAddChar(",")
    lineAddText(pFieldName)
    lineAddChar(",")
    lineAddNum(numValue)

PRI lineTextField(pFieldName, pFieldValue)
' Append one ",name,<token>" field to the record under assembly.
'
' @param pFieldName - pointer to the field name
' @param pFieldValue - pointer to the field's token text

    lineAddChar(",")
    lineAddText(pFieldName)
    lineAddChar(",")
    lineAddText(pFieldValue)

PRI lineEmit()
' Emit the assembled record as exactly one debug line. One debug() statement carries at most
' 255 bytes of debug data; the whole record travels as a single zero-terminated string
' instead so wider records are never silently truncated by that limit.

    debug(zstr_(@lineBuf))

CON { license }

